page RecipeDeployToGithubPages(path: "/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages", title: "Deploy to GitHub Pages — Recipes", description: "GitHub serves a project site under `https://<you>.github.io/<repo>/`, so the build must know that sub-path.") {
    RecipeShell("Deploy to GitHub Pages", summary: "GitHub serves a project site under `https://<you>.github.io/<repo>/`, so the build must know that sub-path.  1. In `webfluent.app.json`, set `\"base_path\": \"/<repo>\"` in `build` and `\"site_url\": \"https://<you>.github.io/<repo>\"` in `meta`. 2. GitHub Pages answers `/contact` with a `301` redirect to `/contact/`. To make the canonical address of every page one it serves without a redirect, also set `\"clean_urls\": \"file\"` (or `\"directory\"`) in `build` ([Content](/recipes)). 3. Add `.github/workflows/pages.yml`:     ```yaml name: Deploy on: push: branches: [main] permissions: contents: read pages: write id-token: write jobs: deploy: runs-on: ubuntu-latest environment: name: github-pages url: $\{\{ steps.deployment.outputs.page_url \}\} steps:          - uses: actions/checkout@v4          - run: curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/master/install.sh | WF_VERSION=v6.0.0 bash          - run: ~/.webfluent/bin/wf build          - uses: actions/upload-pages-artifact@v3 with: path: build          - id: deployment uses: actions/deploy-pages@v4 ```  4. In the repository's **Settings → Pages**, set the source to **GitHub Actions**. 5. Push to `main`.  GitHub Pages serves `404.html` for a path it has no file for. It ignores `_headers`, but the Content-Security-Policy still ships as a `<meta>` tag in every page.  **Verify it:** open the URL the workflow's deploy step prints, then open a page other than the home page directly and reload it. With `clean_urls` set, the address stays as you typed it, with no redirect.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a Docker image", to: "/recipes/docker-image"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Check a deploy", to: "/recipes/check-a-deploy"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to Cloudflare Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/deploy-to-github-pages.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
